The slow section is intentional Monte Carlo rather than certificate search: 200,000 uniformly sampled, column-disjoint candidate matrices. It is progressing at about 2,600 candidates/second; the planted verifier itself is exact and fast. After this pass I’ll use the measured profile to trim only test overhead, not the mandated sample count.
