codex
The current generator’s core construction is sound: every color class is a rational basis because its tail directions form a permutation, and each planted transversal is a basis because its selected quotient directions also form a permutation. I found two audit gaps to correct before rerunning anything: the corruption panel omitted the required empty-answer case, and the canonical-key test checked only one all-at-once relabelling instead of each generator symmetry plus their composition.
